%I A396016 #40 Sep 09 2026 10:58:20
%S A396016 1,1,6,51,1125,83668,23823651,25650746397
%N A396016 Number of nonisomorphic serial binary relations on an n-set having the diamond property.
%C A396016 A binary relation R has the diamond property if xRy and xRz imply that there exists w such that yRw and zRw. Serial means that for every x there exists y such that xRy.
%F A396016 a(n) = (1/n!) * Sum_lambda |C_lambda| * Fix(lambda), where lambda runs over the partitions of n, C_lambda is the conjugacy class in S_n of cycle type lambda, and Fix(lambda) is the number of serial diamond relations fixed by a permutation of cycle type lambda.
%e A396016 For n = 6, the partitions lambda of 6 give the following values of |C_lambda| and Fix(lambda):
%e A396016   1^6: (1, 16823549049)
%e A396016   2 1^4: (15, 20363645)
%e A396016   2^2 1^2: (45, 400785)
%e A396016   2^3: (15, 80445)
%e A396016   3 1^3: (40, 103995)
%e A396016   3 2 1: (120, 2123)
%e A396016   3^2: (40, 2541)
%e A396016   4 1^2: (90, 2053)
%e A396016   4 2: (90, 573)
%e A396016   5 1: (144, 159)
%e A396016   6: (120, 63).
%e A396016 Hence a(6) = (1*16823549049 + 15*20363645 + 45*400785 + 15*80445 + 40*103995 + 120*2123 + 40*2541 + 90*2053 + 90*573 + 144*159 + 120*63)/6! = 23823651.
%Y A396016 Cf. A398789 (labeled serial binary relations having the diamond property).
%K A396016 nonn,hard,more,new
%O A396016 0,3
%A A396016 _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 06 2026
